@startuml act-sync-merge
!include _style.iuml
title SyncEngine.Merge: one item of a sync file

start
:file item (Id = its SyncId in the file);
if (cached item with that SyncId?) then (yes)
  :reuse the cached object\n(keeps tree identity: expansion, selection);
  if (source.AllowSave and cached.LastChange > file.LastChange?) then (yes)
    :keep the cached content\n(a local edit not written back yet);
  else (no)
    :copy title, content, tags,\nshortcuts, paste mode, LastChange\nfrom the file;
  endif
else (no)
  :new Template/Folder with a fresh app Id,\ncontent from the file;
endif
:SyncId = file item's Id;
:merge its children the same way;
:SyncChildren: remove items no longer in the file,\ninsert new ones, move to the file's order;
stop
note right
  The folder root adopts the file root's LastChange, so a
  read-only open re-serializes identically and doesn't
  churn the shared file (OneDrive conflict copies).
  Write-back: BuildFileTree writes items keyed by SyncId
  (new local items get a fresh SyncId), root title "Root".
end note
@enduml
